Problem: marking visited on advance means when stuck need backtrack; simpler: when we advance to v, visited[v]=1, push. If no more available neighbors, pop. Since visited marked on progress, no revisit. Fine — approximation of DFS, always makes forward progress except pops.

If found destino → build path from anteriorArista chain: augment along indices: for idx: forward capacity is `capacidad - flujo`; increase flujo of a and its inverse edge. Need inversa: store in edge as `inversa: number` (index of reverse). When we create pairs, add both.

